+# Incident brief, August–September 2026
+
+Follow-up status as of the 30 September on-call meeting.
+
+## 11 August: ingest stall and full database disk
+
+**Impact:** Customers saw stale dashboards for about 2.5 hours overnight; the database briefly refused writes. No data lost.
+
+**Root cause:** One malformed batch jammed ingest, which retried it endlessly; the retry logs filled the database disk.
+
+**Fix:** A restart that set the batch aside cleared the backlog in six minutes; non-blocking database cleanup and log rotation freed the disk.
+
+**Follow-ups:**
+- Disk alert at 80% (Sunil): done
+- Stop bad batches jamming ingest (Jonas): open, in review
+- Paging escalation after 15 unacknowledged minutes (Elif, Sunil): done
+
+## 21 September: expired API certificate
+
+**Impact:** Public API down 47 minutes on a Monday morning; browsers and nearly all clients could not connect.
+
+**Root cause:** The certificate expired; its renewal job had failed silently since early September, holding an outdated credential.
+
+**Fix:** Certificate renewed and API restarted; renewal job fixed and now alerts on failure.
+
+**Follow-ups:**
+- Reminder 14 days before each expiry (Priya): done
+- Alert on days remaining (Priya): open
+- Expiry check in weekly checklist (Tomasz): open
+- Responders note their steps during incidents (Mara): done
